<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan vegoil rates seen falling.</title>
<headline>Pakistan vegoil rates seen falling.</headline>
<byline>Ibrahim Khan</byline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani vegetable oil prices are likely to fall in the domestic market next week amid rising imports, dealers said on Saturday.</p>
<p>This week RBD palm oil fell to $560 per tonne C&amp;F from $570 last week and soyoil to $565 from $570, a Saulat Enterprises dealer said. Vegoil stocks fell to 143,500 tonnes, including 78,500 tonnes of RBD palm oil and olein, from 159,600 last week.</p>
<p>Stocks in tonnes (Saulat Enterprises estimates):</p>
<p>					     Friday	 May 23</p>
<p>    RBD palm oil/olein		 78,500	 85,000</p>
<p>    Soyoil/sunflower oil	     65,000	 70,000</p>
<p>=====================================================</p>
